// PARAM: --analysis sign
// The concrete result is fixed: foo returns the literal 2, so 0 < y holds.
//
// The combine writes the callee's return slot into the caller's destination
// through the destination's kind conversion, unconditionally. Here that
// conversion is int32 to int32 and the value it converts was produced at
// int32, so it cannot change anything -- but a Sign value carries no kind, so
// nothing at the conversion can see that, and Positive converts to Top.
// Interval answers [2,2] on the same program because its concretization is
// bounded and the conversion is provably the identity on it.
//
// A kind-tagged cell closes this by construction: a value tagged int32
// concretizes inside int32's range, so a conversion to int32 is the identity.
int32 foo() { return 2 }
void main() {
  int32 y;
  y := foo();
  __voblint_check(0 < y) // UNKNOWN
}
